            <ArticleTitle>The rectus abdominis syndrome: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>180-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The case is reported of a patient with a rectus abdominis syndrome. Attention is drawn to the possibility that patients with abdominal pain, in whom no intra-abdominal cause is found, may suffer from this presumed nerve entrapment syndrome. No surgery is required and therapy can be simple.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
